            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I do think we should provide something like a global `<Plug>(nvim-close)` so that users can define a single mapping, and we can define it everywhere applicable. That avoids debates about the actual mapping.\n\nI mean... Mapping `<Plug>(nvim-close)` to `:quit` when there already is `<C-w>q` feels redundant. Most (if not all) its potential usages are for regular windows, dealing with which already should be familiar to most of the users.",
